<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- RUT_GapingDoom — the dead-sarlacc waste pit at tile 2403 (owner, 2026-09-08,
       GAPING_DOOM_SITE_1). A distinct LandmarkDef, not a reskin of sw_DeadSarlacc,
       because THIS instance carries a unique icon: the dead sarlacc with a bright
       green throat, dull at the edges and brightening irregularly toward the centre
       (owner's verbatim art spec). Art generated offline (RUT_GapingDoom.png, alpha
       byte-identical to sw_DeadSarlacc so the footprint is preserved).

       commonality 0 ON PURPOSE — worldgen must never roll it; it is placed only on
       tile 2403 by the world-edit step owed on the item. Description is present-tense,
       what IS: a waste pit and the danger it holds. No past-why (the Rakatan/war-lab
       gating rules), no not-yet-happened plot.

       mutatorChances FIX (GAPING_DOOM_SITE_1, 2026-09-10): the def shipped with no
       mutatorChances at all, which is exactly the live config error seen tonight
       ("LandmarkDef RUT_GapingDoom has no mutators with a chance of 1 or higher").
       Every vanilla/SW LandmarkDef carries a Required="True" entry that drives the
       actual map generation step; sw_DeadSarlaccCave (StarWarsAnimalCollection,
       SW_Buildings_Natural.xml) is exactly the mutator this derives its art from —
       it scatters a DeadSarlacc corpse via GenStep_ScatterThings, which is the correct
       mechanism for "a dead sarlacc used as a waste pit". Reusing it (not copying the
       whole flavor list of Star-Wars-biome mutators alongside it, which don't belong
       in the Cracked Lands) keeps this a minimal, correct fix. -->

  <LandmarkDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
    <defName>RUT_GapingDoom</defName>
    <label>the Gaping Doom</label>
    <description>The corpse of a sarlacc, its throat turned into a pit. The Junkers sell the right to dump into it, and everything the world wants gone goes down: chemical sludge, spent cores, worse. What has pooled at the bottom glows — a hard, wrong green that brightens toward the centre — and the air above it shimmers with heat that has no fire under it. Nothing that goes in comes back, and the ground around it is going quietly poisonous for a day's walk in every direction.</description>
    <iconTexturePath>World/Landmarks/Ashkarr/RUT_GapingDoom</iconTexturePath>
    <atlasSize>(2, 2)</atlasSize>
    <commonality>0</commonality>
    <category>structure</category>
    <nameMaker>NamerLandmark_Ruins</nameMaker>
    <mutatorChances>
      <sw_DeadSarlaccCave MayRequire="Mlie.StarWarsAnimalCollection" Required="True" />
    </mutatorChances>
  </LandmarkDef>

</Defs>
